{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"evidence\":[{\"source\":\"李学勤主编，《字源》，天津古籍出版社、辽宁人民出版社，2012, PDF p. 71 (printed p. 59), original scan pixels supplied as attachment 1\",\"field\":\"茶 headword and entry boundary; direct visual inspection\",\"text\":\"At the lower-left entry, the printed headword is 茶, followed by the parenthetical form 茶 and the reading tú. Its entry text begins “形声字。从艸，齊声。本义是指蓼科植物名。” The entry continues at the top-right of the same page after the lower-left column ends, beginning “引申之亦可比喻苦、痛。” The top running header contains 茶 among other headwords; it is not body text. Page 72 starts unrelated entries and does not continue this 茶 account. Direct scan inspection resolves the body headword as 茶, not 荼.\",\"record_character\":\"茶\",\"kind\":\"locally_inspected_book_scan\",\"url\":\"https://ci.nii.ac.jp/ncid/BB13266817\",\"title\":\"字源 (CiNii catalogue record; publication metadata only)\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"李学勤主编，《字源》，天津古籍出版社、辽宁人民出版社，2012, PDF p. 72 (printed p. 60), original scan pixels supplied as attachment 2\",\"field\":\"page boundary; direct visual inspection\",\"text\":\"The page begins with the tail end of the 薔 entry at the top left, then entries for 藜, 褒, 藩, 荼 and 余 among others. The 荼 entry is a separate headword on this page, not a continuation of the 茶 passage from page 71. This confirms the page 71 top-right paragraph belongs to 茶.\",\"record_character\":\"茶\",\"kind\":\"locally_inspected_book_scan\",\"url\":\"https://ci.nii.ac.jp/ncid/BB13266817\",\"title\":\"字源 (CiNii catalogue record; publication metadata only)\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"李学勤主编，《字源》，天津古籍出版社、辽宁人民出版社，2012, PDF p. 79 (printed p. 67), original scan pixels supplied as attachment 3\",\"field\":\"余 headword and independent account; direct visual inspection\",\"text\":\"The page has a distinct 余 headword with reading yú. Its text calls the graph pictographic, says the oracle-bone form resembles a dwelling supported by a wooden post, and gives an original dwelling sense; it also notes use as a first-person pronoun. This confirms the reported standalone 余 entry. That account does not itself establish sound function in 茶 or 荼.\",\"record_character\":\"余\",\"kind\":\"locally_inspected_book_scan\",\"url\":\"https://ci.nii.ac.jp/ncid/BB13266817\",\"title\":\"字源 (CiNii catalogue record; publication metadata only)\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"臺灣教育部《異體字字典》, Tea headword A03475\",\"field\":\"standard form and component strokes\",\"text\":\"The dictionary identifies standard 茶 as 艹-06-10 and specifies upper 艹 with four strokes and lower 木: the vertical stroke of 木 is unhooked, with left and right strokes disconnected from it. It also quotes an older view that 茶 is a reduced form of 荼, while noting that 茶 and 荼 now have distinct standard forms and different readings/meanings. Thus the literal lower component of current standard 茶 is 木, not 余. Historical phonetic 余 and present lower 木 must not be conflated. The cited page does not itself establish the detailed graphic reduction path.\",\"record_character\":\"茶\",\"kind\":\"authoritative_character_form_dictionary\",\"url\":\"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A03475&powerMode=2\",\"title\":\"A03475 茶 - 教育部《異體字字典》\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"臺灣教育部《異體字字典》, 荼 headword A03494\",\"field\":\"transmitted Shuowen form and phonetic role\",\"text\":\"The entry quotes 大徐本: “苦葵也。从艸，余聲” and 段注本: “苦荼也。从艸，余聲.” This is an explicit sound-role statement for 余 in 荼. It is not an assertion about 余’s role in current 茶, and any comparison must use the pronunciation of 荼 rather than transferring the 茶 reading to the 荼 record.\",\"record_character\":\"荼\",\"kind\":\"authoritative_character_dictionary\",\"url\":\"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?ID=38004&la=0\",\"title\":\"A03494 荼 - 教育部《異體字字典》\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"Chinese University of Hong Kong, Multi-function Chinese Character Database\",\"field\":\"Tea entry analysis\",\"text\":\"The database says 茶 is a later graph, earlier written 荼, analyzed as 艸 plus phonetic 余; it gives the original meaning as tea tree and cites Tang-period usages. This supports the historical analysis but does not justify describing current lower strokes as literally 余.\",\"record_character\":\"茶\",\"kind\":\"dictionary\",\"url\":\"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/search.php?word=%E8%8C%B6\",\"title\":\"漢語多功能字庫：茶\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"}],\"search_audit\":[{\"query\":\"site:zdic.net 茶 字形 艹 余 茶 字源; 茶 字形 余 艹 形声 荼 字源 字典 茶\",\"urls\":[\"https://www.zdic.net/hans/%E8%8C%B6\",\"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?ID=38004&la=0\",\"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A03475&powerMode=2\",\"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/search.php?word=%E8%8C%B6\"],\"outcome\":\"Search performed. Opened the official Taiwan Ministry of Education entries for 茶 and 荼 and the CUHK 茶 entry; inspected their actual character-form and formation statements.\"},{\"query\":\"site:dict.variants.moe.edu.tw 茶 字樣說明 木 余 茶 省文\",\"urls\":[\"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A03475&powerMode=2\",\"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A03475-001\"],\"outcome\":\"Search performed. Opened the official 茶 standard-form page and its 𣘻 variant record. The 茶 page specifies lower 木; the variant page relays an attributed historical proposal that tea 茶 derives from 荼 and later forms, but that remains an attributed account rather than a source-independent proof of detailed reduction.\"}],\"gaps\":[\"[OCR CORRECTION REQUIRED] 字源 PDF p. 71 / printed p. 59, lower-left 茶 headword and main body passage: the provisional page OCR transcribes this body entry as “荼 tú … 形声字。从艸,余声。本义是指苦菜”, but the supplied scan visibly has headword 茶 (with parenthetical 茶), reading tú, and body text “形声字。从艸，齊声。本义是指蓼科植物名”. It is a substantive OCR/record association error, not a one-character headword fix. The attached scan instead prints the phonetic as 齊 (not 余), and the original-meaning wording as 蓼科植物名 (not 苦菜). The entry continues at the top-right of the same PDF p. 71, with “引申之亦可比喻苦、痛”; it does not continue onto PDF p. 72. The page 71 running header occurrence “荔 蒙 范 芳 芭 蕒 薔 苕 茶 菉 蒿 蓬” is a separate header, and 茶 there is not the entry headword. The page 72 separate 荼 entry states “形声字。从艸，余声。本义是指蓼科植物物，嫩叶可食”. This scan reading overturns supplied evidence X-9cd9b69c233df34047e8 and X-06e56e0009261faa45ac insofar as they attach 艸+余 and 苦菜 to the 茶 entry; those records should be retired from the article and replaced only with newly authored scan-supported evidence. Do not retire X-d91d8d379f7dc5089590 or other genuine 荼-entry evidence on this basis.\",\"Affected article-used evidence IDs requiring retirement and fresh authorship/review: X-9cd9b69c233df34047e8 (PDF p. 71 茶 entry is misread as 荼 with 余 phonetic and bitter-vegetable original meaning); X-06e56e0009261faa45ac (describes the same p. 71 continuation as “bitter and painful senses,” but that continuation belongs to 茶, whose preceding p. 71 entry says phonetic 齊 and original plant meaning; its page reference is right but claims need replacement). The supplied article cites both in its summary, formation, history and learner evidence. Preserve the old provenance records; do not revise them in place.\",\"No source-bound record ID for the provisional corpus page 71 was provided in the packet, so the OCR producer must resolve it against its page-id/source hashes. Scan PDF p. 72 directly shows the distinct 荼 headword and a separate 荼 formation statement. The scanned page 71 formation text itself gives 齊 as phonetic; do not silently normalize this printed form or infer 余 from the later discussion.\",\"The article’s current 茶 component form requires correction: current standard lower component is 木 per the official Taiwan Ministry of Education character-form entry. The draft’s historical 余 phonetic analysis may be retained as attributed historical analysis, but should not be represented as the literal lower part of present-day standard 茶. Whether lower 木 is a reduced/replaced descendant of a historical 余 component is a separate historical relationship and should remain qualified; sources inspected here do not fully establish that precise transformation.\",\"Historical 荼 sound record referent mismatch: the supplied component sound comparison pairs 余 with 茶 reading *rlaː, while the claim is scoped to 荼. The official dictionary explicitly assigns 余 as phonetic in 荼 but does not give a same-system Old Chinese reconstruction pair for 荼 and 余. No readily inspected primary same-system pair was established in this pass; do not substitute 茶’s value for 荼 or carry that sound array to the 荼-host record.\",\"The local-primary reading table supplies modern Mandarin 余 yú, 茶 chá, 荼 tú and the official dictionary pages display these current readings, but no primary same-system ancient reconstruction pair for 荼/余 was obtained here.\"]}"}}
